vendor/tinyalsa/asoundlib.h is not tinyalsa upstream code.  It is a
minimal stub written by NAVER Corporation that declares only the
pcm_format enumeration and the pcm_format_to_bits() helper needed at
compile time; the real linking happens against the container's
libtinyalsa.so at runtime.

The CRAS client code that this library links statically comes from
ChromiumOS third_party/adhd and is covered separately by the
BSD-Google license also listed for this package.

